---
import FlowShot from '../FlowShot.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import FlowShot from '../../../components/flow/FlowShot.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../../../components/flow/FlowDetail.astro';
import shotOrganizer from '../../../assets/flow/shots/flow-organizer-shot.webp';
import shotCharts from '../../../assets/flow/shots/flow-charts-shot.webp';
import detailGrid from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-grid.webp';
---
<!-- Chapter 8: Files -->
<section class="border-t border-border/60 bg-surface-raised/30 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="tour-files">
  <div>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
      <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">Your files</p>
      <h3 id="tour-files" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]" data-animate="lead">Plain folders. Plain Markdown. Never a silent overwrite.</h3>
      <p class="of-lede mx-auto mt-5 text-center" data-animate="rise">
        No import step, no library format, no sync silo. The files on disk are the product.
        Collisions refuse instead of overwriting, and Delete goes to the system Trash.
      </p>
    </div>
    {/* Top-left crop, closing the page's rotation. The grid detail is the
        proof that "plain Markdown" survives a real table, over the window
        that shows the documents those tables live in. */}
    <div class="of-stage of-stage--pad-top mt-12" data-animate="plate">
      <FlowShot
        src={shotCharts}
        alt="Flow documents carrying images and tables: a publishing calendar beside an investment memo with a chart image and a metrics table."
        sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 78rem, (min-width: 1024px) 64rem, 100vw"
      />
      <FlowDetail
        class="of-stage__detail of-stage__detail--tl"
        src={detailGrid}
        alt="A Markdown table open in Flow's spreadsheet grid, one cell selected and named R5:C2 in the cell editor bar above it."
        caption="A real grid over a real table · The file on disk stays plain Markdown"
        sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 30rem, (min-width: 1024px) 27rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
        animate
      />
    </div>
    <div class="mx-auto mt-12 grid max-w-5xl items-center gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.08fr_0.92fr]">
      <FlowShot
        src={shotOrganizer}
        alt="Two full-page documents side by side in Flow over a plain folder of Markdown files, with a photograph rendering in place from the folder's own assets."
        caption="Two documents, one plain folder. Pictures render in place, read only from inside the folder you opened."
        crop
        sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 32rem, 100vw"
      />
      <p class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        Folders have no Delete at all, deliberately, because deleting one would take
        everything inside it without showing you what that was. And Flow is sandboxed to
        exactly the folders you selected, so a note cannot reach the rest of your disk by
        naming a path.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
